---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {toHref,readerModels,statusCounts} from '../lib';
---
<Layout title="About | PsychTerms"><div class="article-wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">About this project</p><h1>Words you can build on.</h1><p>PsychTerms is an independent project for psychology and counselling terms. It is being rebuilt from sources with verified permission for reuse. The number of entries will follow the sources and the quality of the work.</p><h2>A preview, not a release</h2><p>Candidate definitions are drafted from the sources shown and published before the two-reader pass. Reviewed means one independent reader passed it; judged means two. The drafter never counts as a reader. Every entry shows its status. Reader models recorded in this preview: {readerModels.join(", ") || "none"}. Numbered-release inclusion is a separate marker and does not change the review status. No numbered release has been published. Fifteen-word copy matches are withheld; shorter wording concerns are labelled for review. Human review happens on the live preview. Vignettes are deferred.</p><p><a href={toHref("downloads/release-note.md")}>Build-written status counts and release note</a> · <a href={toHref("dropped/")}>Dropped entries and reasons</a></p><h2>Sources and rights</h2><p>Eligible original dictionary contributions are offered under CC BY 4.0. Code is MIT licensed. Source-specific attribution and rights remain in force. NLM data is credited to the National Library of Medicine; no endorsement by NLM or any source institution is implied.</p><h2>Use and corrections</h2><p>This is a reference for terms, not a treatment guide or medical advice. Corrections will be accepted through the project repository.</p><p><a href={toHref('downloads/dictionary.json')}>Preview JSON</a> · <a href={toHref('downloads/dictionary.md')}>Preview Markdown</a></p></div></Layout>
